
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <%- include('partials/head.ejs') %>

<body>
<%- include('partials/header.ejs') %>

<main>
    <h2>Conclusion</h2>

    <section>
        <p> Ultimately, good UX design should empower users and cater to their needs, 
            principles, and expectations. While certain design choices can increase user engagement, 
            they should not come at the expense of honesty or fairness. Otherwise, a site's reviews 
            may end up looking like the following:
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>What Users Are Saying</h2>

        <p>
            Here are some fake reviews using Faker.js that demonstrate what could end up happening for
            companies that engage in dark UX practices.
        </p>

        <div class="review-container">

            <% reviews.forEach(review => { %>

                <div class="review-card">

                    <div class="review-user">
                        <img src="<%= review.image %>"
                             alt="Fictional user profile">

                        <h3><%= review.name %></h3>
                    </div>

                    <div class="stars">
                        <%= '★'.repeat(review.rating) %><%= '☆'.repeat(5 - review.rating) %>
                    </div>

                    <p><%= review.feedback %></p>

                    <small><%= review.date %></small>

                </div>

            <% }) %>

        </div>
    </section>

</main>

<%- include('partials/footer.ejs') %>
</body>
</html>